From 34a27b97321a12838c0ee24290ff619a98ae5c00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kirill <sleeply4cat@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 03:12:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] serial: msm_geni: don't enable an error pointer as the
 UART clock

When devm_clk_get_optional() fails, for example because no driver
matches the clock controller, the probe logged it and then passed the
error pointer to clk_enable(), which dereferenced it: a data abort
before any console, so U-Boot just went silent. Carry on without the
clock, as the bootloader left it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015ya7ejvazDaFBN5SE4ttFx
---
 drivers/serial/serial_msm_geni.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/serial/serial_msm_geni.c b/drivers/serial/serial_msm_geni.c
index 30dab2c0..8a77488f 100644
--- a/drivers/serial/serial_msm_geni.c
+++ b/drivers/serial/serial_msm_geni.c
@@ -565,10 +565,13 @@ static int msm_serial_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 	struct clk *clk;
 
 	clk = devm_clk_get_optional(dev, NULL);
-	if (IS_ERR(clk))
+	if (IS_ERR(clk)) {
+		/* e.g. no clock controller driver: keep the clock as the bootloader left it */
 		dev_dbg(dev, "Couldn't find UART clock: %ld", PTR_ERR(clk));
-	else
+		clk = NULL;
+	} else {
 		priv->se = clk;
+	}
 
 	/* Try enable clock */
 	clk_enable(clk);
-- 
